From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:28:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(repository): store v3: per-loop readers, QPSG and
 MEMMODE

One writer connection under wlock, and one read-only connection per
event-loop thread, opened lazily through a thread_local. Every connection
turns SQLITE_DBCONFIG_ENABLE_QPSG on before it prepares anything, so a
bound LIMIT/OFFSET no longer re-prepares the page statement on each call.
The writer keeps WAL, synchronous=NORMAL and busy_timeout, and adds
journal_size_limit=64 MiB. A write reads its row back on the writer under
wlock, so a client sees exactly what it wrote.

DB_PATH=":memory:" is served in one of two modes, MEMMODE: ephemeral
(default), a WAL database in a temp file deleted on close and swept at
the next boot if the process died; or single, one in-RAM connection
whose reads take the writer's lock.

Tests: a reader thread sees the writer's commits on its own connection;
1000 pages with changing bound LIMIT/OFFSET re-prepare 0 times in both
modes (the PLAN 18.2 micro-guard).

Spike S0.4 (docs/spikes/S0.4.md), base of candidates A, B and C.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
